{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "25", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "19", "M": "39", "S": "35"}}, "news": [{"title": "Over 40 underprivileged families to get homes in Karchhana under Mukhyamantri Awas Yojana", "para": "The government is establishing a housing colony in Mungari village to support marginalized communities. This initiative is part of the Mukhyamantri Awas Yojana, aimed at providing permanent housing. Beneficiaries include tribal families and members of the Dharkar community, who currently live in temporary shelters. The project will offer modern amenities such as paved roads and drinking water facilities after construction begins.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/over-40-underprivileged-families-to-get-homes-in-karchhana-under-mukhyamantri-awas-yojana/134478185?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-277390/134478185.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Pay property tax by September 30, avail 10% rebate: Luchina municipal commissioner", "para": "MC commissioner Ojasvi Alankar has taken decisive action by urging officials to speed up the collection of overdue property taxes. Residents are encouraged to pay by September 30 to reap a 10% rebate for the financial year 2026-27. Inspectors and superintendents have been assigned daily targets to ensure effective collection, and zonal suvidha kendras will facilitate assistance on weekends.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/pay-property-tax-by-september-30-avail-10-rebate-luchina-municipal-commissioner/134478149?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-313678/134478149.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Nagpur civic body's panel seeks 50% tax penalty cut for small plots", "para": "Nagpur Municipal Corporation's tax assessment committee has requested a 50% waiver on penalties for property tax arrears. This waiver specifically targets economically weaker sections and small plot owners in the city. The committee expressed concerns about the burden on low-income citizens during the tax recovery process. They urged for verification regarding the issuance of demand bills before issuing warrants.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/nagpur-civic-bodys-panel-seeks-50-tax-penalty-cut-for-small-plots/134478089?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-93282/134478089.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}